## Acetic acid
component-acetic-acid = Acetic acid
    .genitive = acetic acid
component-acetic-acid-description-novice = An acid with a sharp vinegar smell. Table vinegar is a 6–9 % solution of acetic acid in water. The pure acid freezes already at 16.6 °C, which is why it is called “glacial”.
component-acetic-acid-description-school = A weak acid: only a small share of its molecules split into ions in water. It reacts with baking soda and chalk, releasing carbon dioxide.
component-acetic-acid-safety-school = Concentrated acetic acid burns skin and eyes, and its vapour is flammable. Work with it only in goggles and gloves.
component-acetic-acid-model-notes = Evaporation of acetic acid below its boiling point is not modelled yet: no checked vapour-pressure data.
